summary:
  A relayed stream's titles are looked for in its buffer file only, however
  often the buffer has none.

history:
  The relay's Ogg shell holds an Ogg stream's comment tags, and the title
  reader was pointed at the buffer for every stream in one. A plain FLAC
  station has no tags there and sends its titles in ICY. Measured on
  2026-11-11 on two such stations: titles straight off the socket, none in
  25 s through the relay. After three empty reads running the poll goes
  to the ICY reader instead.

target:
  package/contents/ui/TimeshiftLogic.js

find:
      return (icyRefused !== true && misses >= BUFFER_TITLE_MISSES) ? "icy" : "buffer";

replace:
      return (icyRefused !== true && misses >= BUFFER_TITLE_MISSES) ? "buffer" : "buffer";

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_timeshiftlogic.qml::test_titles_come_from_the_buffer_until_it_has_none_three_times.
  Line-neutral.
